  "key_findings": [
    "lr=0.3 from the Nickel-Kiela paper assumes batch_size=10; at batch_size=1024 the per-sample effective lr is too low to train. Scale lr roughly with batch size.",
    "RiemannianAdam (attempts 1-6, indirectly) interacts poorly with the Poincar\u00e9 metric due to per-coordinate adaptive scaling. Use RiemannianSGD.",
    "Manual norm clipping after each optimizer step fights the manifold's exponential map and produces 'clip-jammed' training (attempt 6).",
    "At convergence with RSGD + lr=10, the embedding collapses to a thin annulus near the boundary (mean ~ 0.89, max ~ 0.91). ROOT in this regime gets pushed outward by negative-sampling dynamics.",
    "Root-freeze + hierarchy regularization recovers significant MAP (0.654 -> 0.741) without changing optimizer or core loss.",
    "Whether ROOT is pinned at origin or drifts to ~0.73 does not change MAP in this setup - the bottleneck is in interior-tree edges, not at the root."
